<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.856 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.856 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.2 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due September 18 was 2.856 percent, down from 2.898 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.1 billion of 182-day T-bills due December 18, 1997 was 3.194 percent, down from 3.325 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 357-day T-bills due June 11, 1998 was 3.603 percent, down from 3.807 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$600 million three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$750 million of C$5.7 billion bills due June 26. (Details follow)  </p>
